# Who reviews what.
#
# GitHub requests a review from these people automatically when a pull request
# touches a path they own. Code-owner review is REQUIRED on this repository, so
# one of the names on the matching line has to approve before anything merges.
#
# Maintainer for the HTML and CSS site: @RustyLegend
#
# @pushpam2404 is on every line on purpose:
#   - GitHub does not let anybody approve their own pull request, so a line
#     naming one person would deadlock the moment that person opened one
#   - if the maintainer is unavailable, nothing has to wait for them
#
# The last matching line wins, so the more specific rules are at the bottom.

# Everything, by default
*                       @RustyLegend @pushpam2404

# The site, and the contributor wall that rebuilds itself on merge
/css/                   @RustyLegend @pushpam2404
/js/                    @RustyLegend @pushpam2404
/contributors/          @RustyLegend @pushpam2404

# Automation and the contribution rules. These decide what the checks are, so a
# pull request must not be able to change them with only its own author's
# approval.
/.github/               @pushpam2404
/CONTRIBUTING.md        @pushpam2404
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md     @pushpam2404
/SECURITY.md            @pushpam2404
/LICENSE                @pushpam2404
